        <body>
            <div xml:id="d679">

                <pb facs="0942" n="836" xml:id="pg836"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon quotes the recent correspondence with Guatemala and Salvador.</p>
                <p>Mr. Bacon adds that the Government of the United States is most anxious to do
                    everything possible to preserve peace, but this is evidently impossible without
                    active cooperation of Mexican Government. Directs him to say to President Diaz
                    that the President earnestly wishing to help in avoiding war in Central America,
                    desires to rely largely upon the advice of President Diaz. In response to
                    Minister Merry’s suggestion, the <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> has
                    been ordered to proceed to coast of Salvador.)</p>
            </div>
